.TH "MITSUBISHI\-ECHONET\-DISABLE" "1" "" "mitsubishi\-echonet 0.1.0" "Mitsubishi ECHONET Manual"
.SH NAME
mitsubishi\-echonet\-disable \- disable ECHONET Lite via the /smart endpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mitsubishi\-echonet disable \-\-ip IP [\-\-timeout SECONDS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Sends the disable command to the adapter's /smart endpoint. ECHONET Lite has no authentication: any host on the local network can send these commands. Run only on a trusted network.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-ip IP
adapter IP address on the local network (required)
.TP
.B \-\-timeout SECONDS
seconds to wait (default 3)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
mitsubishi\-echonet disable \-\-ip 192.0.2.10
.RS
Disable ECHONET Lite on the adapter at 192.0.2.10.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed (adapter unreachable or command rejected).
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error (invalid or missing arguments).
